  "tagline": "Apache graph database from Baidu with Gremlin and Cypher, pluggable backends and a distributed store.",
  "description": "Apache HugeGraph is a property-graph database originally built at Baidu and donated to the Apache Software Foundation. It speaks Gremlin and openCypher, stores data in RocksDB for standalone setups or in its own distributed HStore (with a PD placement service) for scale-out, and ships a toolchain for loading, visualization and OLAP computing (Vermeer/Computer). The companion hugegraph-ai project adds GraphRAG and LLM integrations. It is popular in China for large knowledge and risk-control graphs; outside that community documentation is thinner and releases are infrequent (1.7.0 in November 2025).",
